From: jetbee <7734987+jetbee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Keyguard: per-finger E-ink unlock screen for the A6L

On a successful fingerprint authentication, before the unlock is
handled, read Settings.System "fp_unlock_screen" for the authenticated
user: a JSON object mapping fingerprint ids to "0" (LCD) or "1"
(E-ink). For a finger with a choice, tell the E-ink service: as the
wake-up display (setWakeupSourceType(1, 0|4, value == 0)) when the
unlock wakes the device, or as the display type (setDisplayType) when
the device is already interactive. The service is reached by
reflection, falling back to a direct binder lookup when the context
cached a null manager. Errors are logged and the unlock proceeds.

Implemented from cleanroom specs 01-com.hmct.epd.md and
02-epd-service.md (section 5.3).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
